invariant: INV-46
file: mlkem_lanes.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-vector
reason: the NEON product of two coefficient vectors runs on SQDMULH, the
  twiddle factors' form, which saturates where both operands are
  -32768: that product leaves at 16383 where mlk_fqmul gives 16384. Only
  the test's two polynomials of INT16_MIN multiply that pair, so this
  shows the test reaches the one input the form gets wrong. Only an
  arm64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_vector_equiv_test for arm64 and runs it under qemu-aarch64.
  The lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather
  than caught.

--- old
static inline lanes lanes_fqmul_wide(lanes x, lanes y, lanes y_qinv) {
    lanes t = vmulq_s16(x, y_qinv);
--- new
static inline lanes lanes_fqmul_wide(lanes x, lanes y, lanes y_qinv) {
    return lanes_fqmul(x, y, y_qinv);
    lanes t = vmulq_s16(x, y_qinv);
